type: generic
title: "The Scientific Arc of Man's Evolution from the Big Bang to the Human Genome"
version: "333"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23827226
authors:
  - family-names: Berger
    given-names: John Allen
    affiliation: NovagonDNA
abstract: >-
  One arc from the Big Bang to the human genome, described at three layers at
  every stage: the chemical, the biological, and the informational genetic.
  Sulfur and oxygen are treated as a conjugate pair, and inosine as damage the
  cell took up and made into an instrument for reading the code. The unit
  throughout is the nucleotide.
